# Quality bar (Jess)

## AST structure invariants (must never be violated)
- **No self-parenting**: `node.parent === node` is forbidden.
- **No circular parent chains**: traversing `node.parent` must never loop back to the node.
- **No node in its own children**: e.g. a Rules node cannot contain itself.
- Fix violations **at the source** (creation/manipulation), not by filtering during traversal.

## Type safety / node safety
- Do not use `as any` to work around types.
- Do not attach ad-hoc properties to nodes (e.g. `(node as any).foo = ...`).
- If data must flow between phases, use established registries/context patterns; prefer `WeakMap`s keyed by node where appropriate.

## Instrumentation safety (tests/debugging)
- Do **not** `JSON.stringify(...)` AST/parser objects (circular refs).
- Do **not** stringify nodes via `.toString()` / `.toTrimmedString()` for debugging (can affect frame state).
- Log **primitive values only** when tracing.
